					"reach": "C-2",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "10",
							"modifier": 4
						}
					],
					"usage_notes": "Sting (14): thrust 6d impaling (KYOS: 6d+2 impaling) plus follow-up 1d toxic (5 1-hour cycles, resisted by HT-4, -3 HT and -4 DX after loss of 2/3 HP), Reach C-2. Poison: Toxic Attack 1d (Cyclic, 1 hour, 5 cycles, Resistible, +50%; Follow-Up, Sting, +0%; Resistible, HT-4, -10%; Symptoms, 2/3 HP, -3 HT and -4 DX, +55%) Resolve as stated by the construction; the source gives no separate resolution text."
				},
				{
					"id": "AmqcBBi7gmfJUGrQs",
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"base": "5d-1"
					},
					"usage": "Pincers",
					"reach": "C-2",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "10",
							"modifier": 4
						}
					],
					"usage_notes": "Pincers (14): thrust 5d-1 cutting (KYOS: 5d+2 cutting), Reach C-2. The monstrous scorpion can either nip and let go or hold on and grapple the victim in addition to injuring him. Either is an attack that takes full hit location penalties – not halved for grappling. Treat this attack as a bite for these purposes (see Teeth on page 115 of GURPS Martial Arts for details). The pincers give +2 with tasks that require a firm grip (including climbing)."
				}
			]
		}
